From 86be291bec6cc140d708120e33589bd715dbe144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:06:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0018: answer TTL slot 14 from the measured die, or decline

TTL slot 14 (queryGcHardwareInfo) substituted Navi 48's 4x2x8 geometry for any
GFXConfig field that arrived zero, so a boot that measured nothing told Apple the
card had 64 CUs, and a die wider than the struct was truncated instead of refused.
The CU harvest map was never read, so a harvested shader array reported as full.

src/apple/ttl_gc_topo.h makes that decision pure - measured, or declined - and now
uses active_cu_bitmap to emit per-array WGP words. Four refusals return
kTtlUnsupported rather than a guess; the answer publishes as Navi48,TtlGcTopo plus
,TtlGcSe / ,TtlGcShPerSe / ,TtlGcWgpPerSh / ,TtlGcCus so "what did we tell Apple"
is an ioreg read, not a photograph of the log.

tests/ttl_gc_topo_test.cpp: 127 checks, 0 failures. tests/ttl_gc_topo_plant.sh:
35 plants, 0 escaped. Cross-built bundle: 79 objects, 7,247,308 B MH_KEXT_BUNDLE,
no undefined symbols of our own.
